			},
			"date": "2023-10-18T17:18:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Oh dear… scan the article again. TL;DR: Some language servers being pushed have restrictive licensing, which means they can only be used within VSCode.</p><p>I think this will be the standard approach moving forward.</p><p>More info: <a href=\"https://langserver.org/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">langserver.org/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> (fun activity: Search for Microsoft on the page)</p>",
